<title>CANADA: Marleau Lemire says in acquisition talks.</title>
<headline>Marleau Lemire says in acquisition talks.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marleau Lemire Inc said on Monday it has been approached by a third party which is interested in acquiring the independent Canadian investment dealer.</p>
<p>&quot;Discussions are at a preliminary stage and there can be no assurance that any transaction will be concluded,&quot; the Montreal-based company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Marleau Lemire said its board of directors has set up an independent committee to consider the matter.</p>
<p>The company's stock was up 0.05 at 7.35 on the Toronto Stock Exchange before it was halted at 1134 EDT for the announcement.</p>
<p>A TSE official said the stock is scheduled to resume trading at 1315 EDT.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
